{"diagnosis": "Loopback sent 0xa5 with divider 64 but recv_buf_valid/recv_buf_data never delivered 0xa5, giving TRAP: uart timeout, no byte received and tohost FAIL 0xdead. CONE_SLICE has coverage 0/1 with no simpleuart.v refs (only spiflash.v/system.v), so trace wins. Root cause at picosoc/simpleuart.v:59 `cfg_divider[ 7: 1] <= reg_div_di[ 7: 0]` corrupts the low byte so divider 64 is mis-programmed and RX/TX timing never aligns.", "patch_diff": "diff --git a/picosoc/simpleuart.v b/picosoc/simpleuart.v
--- a/picosoc/simpleuart.v
+++ b/picosoc/simpleuart.v
@@ -55,9 +55,9 @@
 	always @(posedge clk) begin
 		if (!resetn) begin
 			cfg_divider <= DEFAULT_DIV;
 		end else begin
-			if (reg_div_we[0]) cfg_divider[ 7: 1] <= reg_div_di[ 7: 0];
+			if (reg_div_we[0]) cfg_divider[ 7: 0] <= reg_div_di[ 7: 0];
 			if (reg_div_we[1]) cfg_divider[15: 8] <= reg_div_di[15: 8];
 			if (reg_div_we[2]) cfg_divider[23:16] <= reg_div_di[23:16];
 			if (reg_div_we[3]) cfg_divider[31:24] <= reg_div_di[31:24];
 		end
 	end", "expected": "tohost: PASS (FAIL 0xdead cleared), uart loopback 0xa5 received with no timeout"}

